# B6 hosts statement gate: freeze check of the eight existing files touched

Tool: `bash <S>/tools/leanelab.sh <S>/wt-g5b6 <S>/oleans-f8 <file>` (a direct `lean` call
inside the worktree, no `-o`, no olean written). Worktree: the read-only checkout `wt-g5b6`
at campaign commit `1781a230d2410ae2a09fbb961fe644512a6ba3c0` (the worktree's HEAD file); olean snapshot `oleans-f8`
(all of TCSlib at that commit, and Mathlib). Toolchain `leanprover/lean4:v4.25.0`.
<OUT> is this pack's scratch directory, <S> the scratchpad. Run: 2026-10-14 03:24 UTC.

`python3 -I <OUT>/scripts/freeze.py <worktree file> <patched file> <allowed statement changes>
<allowed body changes>`: every declaration's statement (comment-stripped, up to the top-level
`:=`), body and docstring compared; a statement or body change outside the allowances fails.
The allowances are exactly the user's decisions B1 (`space_universal`) and B3 (the S1b
re-pointing), and the one proof re-derivation (`exists_codeTM`, to build the relabelling once).

